    ],
    "title": "**\"No automated rename repair\"**",
    "text": "**\"No automated rename repair\"**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800E' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> misdiagnosed — a rename adds an anchor rather than replacing one, so an old reference doesn't break at rename time; there's nothing to repair, only a later cleanup once it's actually safe. See [Architecture](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8002).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800B",
