    ],
    "title": "**2026-09-09: cross-artifact link staleness**",
    "text": "**2026-09-09: cross-artifact link staleness**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBZ769800C' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> Live editing of this very concern's own docs surfaced a second gap: `discussion/linking.md` linked to a heading just added to `design/linking.md` in the same pass, and that link resolved against whichever of the two artifacts' graph states happened to be current at ingestion time — an artifact whose own text never changes has nothing to trigger a fresh link-resolution pass, so a dangling reference stayed dangling even after its target came into existence, fixable only by manually corrupting `ingestedHash` to force a re-ingest. `resolveBlockLinks` (`apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`) now stashes every code a block fails to resolve — including a `#fragment` form that's merely routine-unresolved, not warned as dangling — as a `danglingRef` prop on its own referring `ArtifactNode`, rewritten wholesale on every ingestion. `kg:ingest` (`kgIngest.ts`'s `runIngest`) gained a closing sweep, `retryDanglingRefs`: after the requested artifacts and folder tree are settled, every stashed code across every live artifact is retried against the current graph, and any artifact with at least one now-resolvable code is force-reingested via a new `ingestFromDisk`/`ingestArtifact` parameter, `bypassUnchangedCheck` — added deliberately separate from just clearing `ingestedHash`, since that field is also how `ingestFromDisk` decides whether to reconcile against existing content or fresh-mint every block as brand new (see [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR008)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698004",
