    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 1** (landed)",
    "text": "**Slice 1** (landed): <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG003' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> the mechanism itself — lead-in-term title extraction, recognizing `aperas://`/`#fragment` link forms, and id-anchor emission (both headings and list items).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 2** (landed)",
    "text": "**Slice 2** (landed): <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG004' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> completes the toolset for working directly on Apeiron — collision rejection at ingestion, the cleanup pass, and folding Slice 1's own verification into `verify.ts`. Corpus-wide rollout of the convention (correcting non-compliant colon lead-ins, migrating old-style `[[deep-path]]` links) is a separate topic, not detailed here.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77EG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
