    "title": "00CDC0RFD8009",
    "text": "**Lead-in-term title extraction** (`astParser.ts`) — landed as `findLeadInColonOffset`/`extractLeadInTitle`, revised after live corpus ingestion surfaced real corruption from the originally-planned raw-character scan; see [Lead-In Term Detection](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000) for the settled rule and [Finding the real lead-in colon](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR000) for why.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0005",
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0006",
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0007",
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0008",
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0009",
      "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F000A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RFD800A",
    "text": "Walks the block's own parsed inline mdast nodes, not raw characters — a candidate colon (or `：` for Japanese) must sit in plain text, never inside `inlineCode` or a `strong`/`emphasis` span.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RFD800B",
    "text": "Gated by a length cap (10 words / 20 Japanese characters) and, for a space-delimited script, a following-whitespace check — both needed on top of the code/bold exclusion, not instead of it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RFD800C",
    "text": "Which script's rules apply comes from a new `lang: en|ja|vi` frontmatter field (`extractLangFromFrontmatter`), threaded through both parsing and projection.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RFD800D",
    "text": "No qualifying colon found → keep the existing `blockId` fallback (astParser.ts:274) unchanged.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDC0RFD800E",
    "text": "`text` is left completely unmodified by this — `title` is a read-only label extracted from (not cut out of) the span before the colon. Safe because `serializeListItem`/the paragraph projection case already render from `text` alone and never touch a list item's/paragraph's `title`, so there's nothing to reassemble at projection.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F000A:links:Link:00CDBZ7800000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
