      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG003",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80002",
    "type": "list",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80004",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80004:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80004:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0000:props:StringProp:00CDDBQ9G0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "16"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Discussion**",
    "text": "**Discussion**: [Motivation — the mixing problem](../discussion/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002) — rationale for adopting block-based separation, evidenced by the pre-Phase-1.1 corpus.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80005:links:Link:00CDDBQ9G0002:props:StringProp:00CDDBQ9G8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Issues**",
    "text": "**Issues**: [Resolved: Context/Discussion boundary](../issues/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004) — Context conflicted with Discussion's \"motivation\"; resolved by defining Context as a factual index, not narrative.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**History**",
    "text": "**History**: to be updated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007:props:StringProp:00CDD68EQR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007:props:StringProp:00CDD68EQR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Architecture",
    "text": "To achieve pure Perata (clean projections for the reader), the storage layer must adopt a **Block-Based Separation of Concerns**. Instead of one mixed file, the Apeiron stores strictly isolated documents (or trees):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E80009",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000A",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000B",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000C",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG008",
    "text": "**Design Docs:** Pure architectural specifications, data models, and rules.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG009",
    "text": "**Issue Docs:** Bug reports, architectural gaps, and pending fixes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG00A",
    "text": "**Planning Docs:** Implementation plans, task breakdowns, and step-by-step execution guides.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG00B",
    "text": "**History/Status Docs:** What was implemented, when it was verified, and milestones.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG00C",
    "text": "**Discussion Docs:** Rejected ideas, motivation, and theoretical context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG00D",
    "text": "This guarantees that a reader parsing the \"Design Doc\" sees *only* the design, without needing complex transducers to strip out bug reports and history logs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Topology",
    "text": "A rigid physical directory structure inevitably fails because software development requires different lenses at different times (e.g., building a feature vs. fixing a cross-cutting bug). Because all edits happen on the unbounded tree (Apeiron), we optimize physical storage for the **Reader** (stability) and use TreeViews/Freeflow documents for the **Agent** (dynamic tasks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Physical Storage: Concern-Centric",
    "text": "At the file-system layer, artifacts are strictly grouped by concern. This forms the system-wide documentation naturally.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RG00G",
    "text": "```text\nartifacts/\n  ├── design/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Pure Perata: Architecture, Models, Specs)\n  │   └── treeview.md\n  ├── issues/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Bugs, gaps, pending tasks)\n  │   └── network.md\n  ├── planning/\n  │   └── crud.md                 (Implementation plans, step-by-step execution guides)\n  ├── history/\n  │   └── crud.md                 (Implementation status, log of changes)\n  └── discussion/\n      └── crud.md                 (Rationale, rejected ideas, unstructured thought)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000F",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H:props:StringProp:00CDD68ERR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H:props:StringProp:00CDD68ERR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Document-Level Skeletons",
    "text": "To ensure uniformity across the corpus, each concern document should follow a strict top-level heading structure. Standardizing these paths (e.g., `design/crud.md/Data-Model`) allows the agent to reliably address them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000J",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000N",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000Q",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000"
    ]
  },
  {
