  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000:props:StringProp:00CDD68ESG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000:props:StringProp:00CDD68ESG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**History Docs (`history/*.md`)**",
    "text": "**History Docs (`history/*.md`)**: <a name='id/BlockNode:00CDD68E88000' class='aperas-anchor aperas-id'></a> Chronological or state-based facts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR005",
    "text": "`# Current Status`, `# Milestones`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Workflows",
    "text": "The strict physical isolation of concerns is necessary for long-term health, but it is hostile to the creative process. The Aperas workflow bridges this gap by using a **Freeflow Artifact** in the `discussion/` directory as the active workspace.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88003",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR007",
    "text": "When starting a task, the agent doesn't jump between `design.md` and `issues.md`. They create a freeflow discussion document, which serves two simultaneous purposes:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The Dashboard (Context Assembly)",
    "text": "The top of the freeflow document acts as a control panel. The agent authors structural links to all the formal blocks across the corpus that are relevant to the current task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88005",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88006",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR009",
    "text": "**`discussion/crud-reconciliation-task.md`**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00A",
    "text": "```markdown\n# CRUD Reconciliation Task\n\n## Dashboard\n[Current Architecture](../design/crud.md/Architecture)\n[The Bug Report](../issues/crud.md/Open-Issues/Nowhere-Problem)\n[The Plan](../planning/crud.md/Implementation-Plan)\n[Status](../history/crud.md/Current-Status)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00B",
    "text": "*(By linking these, the agent anchors the formal state into their workspace. When unfolded via `TreeView`, it projects all these scattered formal blocks into a single localized lens).*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The Scratchpad (Freeflow Authoring)",
    "text": "Beneath the dashboard, the agent dumps unstructured, messy thoughts exactly as they do today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E88009",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00D",
    "text": "```markdown\n## Brainstorming\nSo the issue happens because the parent node is missing.\nIf we use a placeholder flag on the node, it could reconcile safely...\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00E",
    "text": "This is pure Apeiron. It is unbounded, unstructured, and safe from strict schema rules. It exists only in the discussion concern.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Crystallization (The Update Loop)",
    "text": "Eventually, the brainstorming yields a concrete decision. The thought *crystallizes* from a messy idea into a formal architectural rule, or a formal task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800C",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00G",
    "text": "Instead of leaving that crystallized rule buried in the freeflow text, the agent projects it back to the formal block using the CRUD surface:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00H",
    "text": "```bash\n# Push the crystallized rule to the formal design block\nkg:update design/crud.md/Architecture --text \"A placeholder is a flag, not a distinct kind...\"\n\n# Push the execution steps to the formal planning block\nkg:update planning/crud.md/Task-Breakdown --text \"- [ ] Add placeholder flag to nodes\\n- [ ] Reconcile missing parents\"\n\n# Push the resolution status to the formal history block\nkg:update history/crud.md/Current-Status --text \"Resolved Nowhere Problem via placeholder flags.\"\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E:props:StringProp:00CDD68ET8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E:props:StringProp:00CDD68ETG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "### The Resulting Ecosystem",
    "text": "This creates a perfect symbiosis:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E88002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800G",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00K",
    "text": "The **Freeflow Document** (in `discussion/`) retains the entire historical journey of the thought process, the rejected ideas, and the dashboard of links that defined the task context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00M",
    "text": "The **Formal Documents** (in `design/`, `issues/`, `planning/`, `history/`) remain pristine and strictly isolated, containing only the crystallized reality of the system.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBQ8RR00N",
    "text": "The **Agent** navigates the graph easily, using the freeflow document as a central hub that fans out to the formal specs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Documentation Architecture — Discussion",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDD68DSG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Motivation: The Mixing Problem",
    "text": "Currently, documents in `AperasKG/artifacts/` are massive mixtures of completely different logical concerns. Looking at actual project files (e.g., `Aperas-crud-design.md` and `Aperas-treeview-design.md`), the writer often mixes everything into a single document and sometimes even the same paragraph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
      "BlockNode:00CDDBVXAR002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003:props:StringProp:00CDD68FCR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003:props:StringProp:00CDD68FCR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG003",
    "text": "No transducer or adapter can automatically untangle this. A single artifact today contains:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8005",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8006",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8007",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG004",
    "text": "**Core Design:** The actual specification (e.g., `3. Core model: placeholder is a flag`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG005",
    "text": "**Issues & Gaps:** Bugs discovered live during implementation (e.g., `6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAG006",
    "text": "**History & Status:** Implementation progress and verification records (e.g., `Status: implemented, live-verified against a synthetic graph`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAR000",
    "text": "**Discussion & Rationale:** Why something was built a certain way, or rejected (e.g., `12. Considered and rejected`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDDBVXAR001",
    "text": "**Implementation Details:** Notes to self about code structure.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Documentation — Issues",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDD68DSG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0002",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0003",
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Open Issues",
    "text": "None.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Pending Tasks",
    "text": "None.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Resolved",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0005:props:StringProp:00CDD68G38000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0005:props:StringProp:00CDD68G38001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBQ9J0005",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0004",
    "type": "list",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006:links:Link:00CDDBQA60000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006:links:Link:00CDDBQA60000:props:StringProp:00CDDBQA60001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "491"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006:links:Link:00CDDBQA60002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0006:links:Link:00CDDBQA60002:props:StringProp:00CDDBQA60003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "560"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBQ9J0006",
    "text": "**Context/Discussion boundary was undefined.** `design.md`'s skeleton named `# Context` as a heading, while the concern taxonomy filed \"motivation\" under Discussion Docs — with no stated line between the two, Context could silently regrow into narrative.\n    Resolved by defining `# Context` as a factual index: a link plus a brief, non-argumentative summary per linked doc (what exists, not why). Rationale and narrative stay in the linked `discussion.md`, never inline in `design.md`. See [Context](../design/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68E80002) and [Document-Level Skeletons](../design/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68E8000H).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68FE0005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDBVXAR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDBVXAR002:links:Link:00CDDBVXXG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68E80007",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDBVXAR002:links:Link:00CDDBVXXG000:props:StringProp:00CDDBVXXR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "79"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CDDBVXAR002",
    "text": "This is the evidence base for adopting block-based separation of concerns (see [Architecture](../design/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68E80007)): splitting design, issues, planning, history, and discussion into strictly isolated documents so a reader parsing a Design doc sees only the design.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDD68EV8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXH8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# CLI Packaging — Design",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CDDTBJBG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG000",
      "BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Context",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXH8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG001",
